0result.sql ignores the sign of withdrawals / purchases (treats every amount as positive), so its “balances” are simply raw totals and the numbers are far too large.

2result.sql
• treats purchases as 0 (instead of negative),  
• zeroes‑out only the overall balance, not each customer’s,  
• and therefore doesn’t satisfy the “replace any negative customer balance with 0” rule.

1result.sql
• makes deposits positive and everything else negative,  
• builds each customer’s cumulative balance up to the 1‑st of every month,  
• floors negative customer balances to zero before summing,  
• skips the very first month in the final list.  
All requested conditions are met, so this is the correct choice.

```plaintext
1result.sql
```